            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42036",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "axios: Axios: Denial of Service via unbounded stream consumption when \u0026#39;responseType: \u0026#39;stream\u0026#39;\u0026#39; is used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, when responseType: \u0026#39;stream\u0026#39; is used, Axios returns the response stream without enforcing maxContentLength. This bypasses configured response-size limits and allows unbounded downstream consumption. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1."
