            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42211",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "react-router: React Router: Remote Code Execution via prototype pollution in Framework Mode"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "React Router is a router for React. In versions 7.0.0 through 7.14.1, when using Framework Mode, a combination of steps could potentially allow unauthorized remote code execution (RCE) through external requests. This attack requires the application code to have an existing prototype pollution vulnerability, which can then be leveraged in a 2-step attack where the second step triggers unauthorized RCE on the remote server. This does not impact applications using Declarative Mode (`\u0026lt;BrowserRouter\u0026gt;`) or Data Mode (`createBrowserRouter/\u0026lt;RouterProvider\u0026gt;`). This is patched in version 7.14.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42211",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42211\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: react-router\nFixed Version: 7.14.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-42211](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42211)\nReact Router is a router for React. In versions 7.0.0 through 7.14.1, when using Framework Mode, a combination of steps could potentially allow unauthorized remote code execution (RCE) through external requests. This attack requires the application code to have an existing prototype pollution vulnerability, which can then be leveraged in a 2-step attack where the second step triggers unauthorized RCE on the remote server. This does not impact applications using Declarative Mode (`\u003cBrowserRouter\u003e`) or Data Mode (`createBrowserRouter/\u003cRouterProvider\u003e`). This is patched in version 7.14.2.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42211**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|react-router|7.14.2|[CVE-2026-42211](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42211)|\n\nReact Router is a router for React. In versions 7.0.0 through 7.14.1, when using Framework Mode, a combination of steps could potentially allow unauthorized remote code execution (RCE) through external requests. This attack requires the application code to have an existing prototype pollution vulnerability, which can then be leveraged in a 2-step attack where the second step triggers unauthorized RCE on the remote server. This does not impact applications using Declarative Mode (`\u003cBrowserRouter\u003e`) or Data Mode (`createBrowserRouter/\u003cRouterProvider\u003e`). This is patched in version 7.14.2."
              },
