            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42342",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "react-router: @remix-run/server-runtime: React Router / Remix: Denial of Service via unbounded path expansion in __manifest endpoint"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "React Router is a router for React. In versions 7.0.0 through 7.14.x of react-router and versions 2.10.0 through 2.17.4 of @remix-run/server-runtime, certain crafted requests can consume disproportionate server resources via unbounded path expansion in the __manifest endpoint, resulting in response time degradation and/or service unavailability for end users. This affects React Router Framework Mode applications as well as Remix applications. This does not impact applications using Declarative Mode (`\u0026lt;BrowserRouter\u0026gt;`) or Data Mode (`createBrowserRouter/\u0026lt;RouterProvider\u0026gt;`). This is patched in react-router version 7.15.0 and @remix-run/server-runtime version 2.17.5."
