              "id": "CVE-2026-22030",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "react-router: React Router CSRF in Action/Server Action Request Processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "React Router is a router for React. In @remix-run/server-runtime version prior to 2.17.3. and react-router 7.0.0 through 7.11.0, React Router (or Remix v2) is vulnerable to CSRF attacks on document POST requests to UI routes when using server-side route action handlers in Framework Mode, or when using React Server Actions in the new unstable RSC modes. There is no impact if Declarative Mode (\u0026lt;BrowserRouter\u0026gt;) or Data Mode (createBrowserRouter/\u0026lt;RouterProvider\u0026gt;) is being used. This issue has been patched in @remix-run/server-runtime version 2.17.3 and react-router version 7.12.0."
