              "id": "CVE-2026-33244",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "react-router: React Router: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) via improper HTTP Location header neutralization"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "React Router is a router for React. In versions 7.5.1 through 7.13.1, when using Framework Mode with pre-rendering enabled, improper neutralization of the HTTP `Location` header value can permit Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) in the statically generated HTML files if the redirect location comes from an untrusted source. This does not impact applications using Declarative Mode (`\u0026lt;BrowserRouter\u0026gt;`) or Data Mode (`createBrowserRouter/\u0026lt;RouterProvider\u0026gt;`). This is patched in version 7.13.2."
